{"id":"fishermens-trail","title":"Rota Vicentina: Fishermen's Trail","who":"Classic route · Portugal's wild Atlantic coast on foot","when":"September to June (summer is hot)","vehicle":"On foot, 4–13 days","kind":"walk","color":"#0e7490","summary":"A cliff-top path in soft sand along the south-west coast of Portugal, used by fishermen to reach their spots: storks nesting on sea stacks, hidden beaches, river mouths and whitewashed villages, through the Southwest Alentejo and Vicentine Coast Natural Park. The classic four stages run Porto Covo to Odeceixe; it now continues to the Cape St Vincent. Cliff edges collapse in places: keep to the marked path and its diversions.","sources":[{"label":"Rota Vicentina: update on the risk of landslides on the Fishermen's Trail","url":"https://blog.rotavicentina.com/en/update-on-the-risk-of-landslides-on-the-fishermens-trail/"},{"label":"Monkey's Tale: hiking the Fishermen's Trail, northern section (January 2025)","url":"https://monkeystale.ca/2025/01/21/hiking-the-fishermens-trail-the-northern-section/"},{"label":"Rota Vicentina: Fishermen's Trail","url":"https://blog.rotavicentina.com/en/tag/fishermens-trail"}],"approximate":"The classic stages; the path follows the coast near the line shown.","km":129,"bbox":[-8.9965,37.0081,-8.76,37.8518],"stops":[{"name":"Porto Covo","place":"Porto Covo, Portugal","at":[37.8517,-8.7918],"text":"A white fishing village and the start, the island of Pessegueiro offshore.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Porto_Covo_January_2011-1a.jpg/500px-Porto_Covo_January_2011-1a.jpg","page":"Porto Covo","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Porto_Covo_January_2011-1a.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Vila Nova de Milfontes","place":"Vila Nova de Milfontes, Portugal","at":[37.7253,-8.7823],"text":"Sand dunes and cliffs to the mouth of the Mira river.","source":{"label":"Monkey's Tale (2025)","url":"https://monkeystale.ca/2025/01/21/hiking-the-fishermens-trail-the-northern-section/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Vila_Nova_de_Milfontes.jpg/500px-Vila_Nova_de_Milfontes.jpg","page":"Vila Nova de Milfontes","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vila_Nova_de_Milfontes.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Almograve","place":"Almograve, Portugal","at":[37.6529,-8.7928],"text":"Dark schist cliffs and beaches below."},{"name":"Zambujeira do Mar","place":"Zambujeira do Mar, Portugal","at":[37.5256,-8.7848],"text":"Past Cabo Sardão, where white storks nest on the sea cliffs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Zambujeira.jpg/500px-Zambujeira.jpg","page":"Zambujeira do Mar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zambujeira.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Odeceixe","place":"Odeceixe, Portugal","at":[37.4332,-8.7702],"text":"Across the Seixe river into the Algarve, a beach in a river bend.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Odeceixe553.jpg/500px-Odeceixe553.jpg","page":"Odeceixe","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Odeceixe553.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Aljezur","place":"Aljezur, Portugal","at":[37.3152,-8.8041],"text":"A Moorish castle above the town.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Vista_geral_de_Aljezur_-_14-03-2020.jpg/500px-Vista_geral_de_Aljezur_-_14-03-2020.jpg","page":"Aljezur","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_geral_de_Aljezur_-_14-03-2020.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Carrapateira","place":"Carrapateira, Portugal","at":[37.184,-8.895],"text":"Surf beaches at Bordeira and Amado."},{"name":"Cape St Vincent","place":"Cabo de São Vicente","at":[37.0226,-8.9966],"text":"The south-west corner of Europe, once thought the